  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1052 PM CDT MON OCT 19 2026\n\nDry northwest to northerly flow aloft persists through the week,\nbetween ridging over the Southern Plains and troughing along the\nEast Coast. At the surface, high pressure over the eastern CONUS\nmaintains a dry continental air mass, while a surface low moves\nslowly northeastward offshore of the Outer Banks. Northeasterly\nflow trajectories at the surface result in cool nights and\ntemperatures near or only slightly above average. Towards the\nweekend, the low pressure system over the western Atlantic exits,\nwhile a cutoff low forms near Cuba. This allows the mid-level\nsubtropical ridge to build eastward, but a strengthening CAD\nwedge in the wake of the Atlantic system helps to offset this,\nmaintaining pleasant temperatures.\n\n32/JDavis",
